node-exporter: add the pressure, stat, schedstat, processes and vmstat
collectors and the cpu collector's cpu.info option, so the stress tool's
scrape carries PSI, tasks blocked on I/O, run-queue wait, thread counts
per state, page-cache dirtying and writeback, and the CPU model. With
load1 they help tell CPU queueing, I/O wait and other uninterruptible
sleep apart, and the CPU model tells two runs on different host
generations apart in the report.

run-test.sh applies this to the agent-sandbox checkout after the tag is
checked out, and skips it once a tag carries the lines.

diff --git a/test/benchmarks/scenarios/benchmarks-kops-gcp/node-exporter.yaml b/test/benchmarks/scenarios/benchmarks-kops-gcp/node-exporter.yaml
index 0911c2a..c7d1702 100644
--- a/test/benchmarks/scenarios/benchmarks-kops-gcp/node-exporter.yaml
+++ b/test/benchmarks/scenarios/benchmarks-kops-gcp/node-exporter.yaml
@@ -60,6 +60,13 @@ spec:
             - --collector.meminfo
             - --collector.diskstats
             - --collector.loadavg
+            - --collector.pressure
+            - --collector.stat
+            - --collector.schedstat
+            - --collector.processes
+            - --collector.cpu.info
+            - --collector.vmstat
+            - --collector.vmstat.fields=^(oom_kill|pgpg|pswp|pg.*fault|nr_dirt|nr_written|nr_writeback).*
             - --collector.textfile
             - --collector.textfile.directory=/textfile
           ports:
